      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Google Cloud KMS**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud KMS for this task. The next step is implementing the encryption function within the `encrypt_payload.py` script. I'm focusing on integrating the Google Cloud KMS SDK to manage and utilize a key for encrypting the plaintext payload.\n\n\n**Defining Encryption Workflow**\n\nI've outlined the encryption workflow within `encrypt_payload.py`. The script will use the Google Cloud KMS SDK, specifically `google.cloud.kms_v1`. I am building out the encryption logic, which will use project ID, location ID, key ring ID, key ID, and the plaintext payload. The function will take these inputs and return the encrypted ciphertext.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865962536,
          "start": 1789865959796
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc53217400130zyh1Ybh5XgSW",
